Here are some commonly used commands and annotations in the Spring Framework:

### Core Annotations and Commands

1. **@Component**: Marks a Java class as a bean.
   ```java
   @Component
   public class MyComponent {
       // code here
   }
   ```

2. **@Service**: A specialized version of @Component, used for service layer classes.
   ```java
   @Service
   public class MyService {
       // service code here
   }
   ```

3. **@Repository**: A specialized version of @Component, used for DAO (Data Access Object) classes.
   ```java
   @Repository
   public class MyRepository {
       // data access code here
   }
   ```

4. **@Controller**: Marks a class as a Spring MVC controller.
   ```java
   @Controller
   public class MyController {
       // controller code here
   }
   ```

5. **@RestController**: A combination of @Controller and @ResponseBody, used for RESTful web services.
   ```java
   @RestController
   public class MyRestController {
       @GetMapping("/hello")
       public String hello() {
           return "Hello, World!";
       }
   }
   ```

6. **@Autowired**: Automatically injects dependencies.
   ```java
   @Service
   public class MyService {
       @Autowired
       private MyRepository repository;
   }
   ```

7. **@Qualifier**: Specifies which bean to inject when there are multiple beans of the same type.
   ```java
   @Service
   public class MyService {
       @Autowired
       @Qualifier("mySpecificBean")
       private MyRepository repository;
   }
   ```

8. **@Value**: Injects values from properties files.
   ```java
   @Component
   public class MyComponent {
       @Value("${my.property}")
       private String myProperty;
   }
   ```

9. **@Configuration**: Indicates that a class declares one or more @Bean methods.
   ```java
   @Configuration
   public class MyConfig {
       @Bean
       public MyBean myBean() {
           return new MyBean();
       }
   }
   ```

10. **@Bean**: Marks a method as a bean producer.
    ```java
    @Bean
    public MyBean myBean() {
        return new MyBean();
    }
    ```

11. **@PropertySource**: Specifies the location of properties files.
    ```java
    @Configuration
    @PropertySource("classpath:application.properties")
    public class MyConfig {
        // configuration code here
    }
    ```

### Spring Boot Specific Annotations

1. **@SpringBootApplication**: A combination of @Configuration, @EnableAutoConfiguration, and @ComponentScan.
   ```java
   @SpringBootApplication
   public class Application {
       public static void main(String[] args) {
           SpringApplication.run(Application.class, args);
       }
   }
   ```

2. **application.properties**: Commonly used properties file for configuration.
   ```properties
   server.port=8080
   spring.datasource.url=jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/mydb
   spring.datasource.username=root
   spring.datasource.password=password
   ```

3. **SpringApplication.run()**: Bootstraps a Spring application from the main method.
   ```java
   SpringApplication.run(Application.class, args);
   ```

### Spring Data JPA

1. **@Entity**: Marks a class as a JPA entity.
   ```java
   @Entity
   public class User {
       @Id
       @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
       private Long id;
       private String name;
       // getters and setters
   }
   ```

2. **@Repository**: Indicates that a class is a repository.
   ```java
   @Repository
   public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User, Long> {
       List<User> findByName(String name);
   }
   ```

### Spring Security

1. **@EnableWebSecurity**: Enables Spring Security’s web security support.
   ```java
   @Configuration
   @EnableWebSecurity
   public class WebSecurityConfig extends WebSecurityConfigurerAdapter {
       @Override
       protected void configure(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
           http
               .authorizeRequests()
               .anyRequest().authenticated()
               .and()
               .formLogin().permitAll();
       }
   }
   ```

2. **UserDetailsService**: Custom implementation for loading user-specific data.
   ```java
   @Service
   public class MyUserDetailsService implements UserDetailsService {
       @Override
       public UserDetails loadUserByUsername(String username) throws UsernameNotFoundException {
           // load user from database
       }
   }
   ```

### Transaction Management

1. **@Transactional**: Marks a method or class as transactional.
   ```java
   @Service
   public class MyService {
       @Transactional
       public void performTransaction() {
           // transactional code here
       }
   }
   ```

### Scheduling

1. **@EnableScheduling**: Enables Spring’s scheduled task execution capability.
   ```java
   @Configuration
   @EnableScheduling
   public class SchedulingConfig {
       // scheduling configuration
   }
   ```

2. **@Scheduled**: Schedules a method to be executed at fixed intervals.
   ```java
   @Component
   public class ScheduledTasks {
       @Scheduled(fixedRate = 5000)
