The error indicates a circular dependency between your `SecurityConfig`, `JwtRequestFilter`, and `UserService` beans. This happens because `SecurityConfig` and `JwtRequestFilter` both depend on `UserService`, which also depends on `PasswordEncoder`, which is defined in `SecurityConfig`.

One way to break this cycle is to refactor the dependency injection so that `JwtRequestFilter` does not directly depend on `UserService`. Instead, we can use `AuthenticationManager` to handle authentication.

### Updated `JwtRequestFilter.java`

Refactor `JwtRequestFilter` to use `AuthenticationManager` instead of directly injecting `UserService`.

