Here's a React functional component with an input field and a search button that also shows previously searched values:

```jsx
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const SearchComponent = () => {
  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('');
  const [searchHistory, setSearchHistory] = useState([]);

  const handleInputChange = (e) => {
    setInputValue(e.target.value);
  };

  const handleSearch = () => {
    if (inputValue.trim() !== '') {
      setSearchHistory([...searchHistory, inputValue]);
      setInputValue(''); // Clear input after search
    }
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input 
        type="text" 
        value={inputValue} 
        onChange={handleInputChange} 
        list="search-history"
      />
      <button onClick={handleSearch}>Search</button>

      <datalist id="search-history">
        {searchHistory.map((item, index) => (
          <option key={index} value={item} />
        ))}
      </datalist>
    </div>
  );
};

export default SearchComponent;
```

In this component:
- `inputValue` holds the current value of the input field.
- `searchHistory` keeps track of the previously searched values.
- `handleInputChange` updates the `inputValue` state when the input field changes.
- `handleSearch` adds the current `inputValue` to the `searchHistory` and clears the input field.

The `datalist` element allows the input to show previously searched values as suggestions.

