- We've added a `<select>` element that allows users to choose linked tasks from a dropdown list. The selected task IDs are stored in the `linkedTasks` property of the form data.

- We assume that `tasks` is an array of task objects containing information about all available tasks. You can pass this array as a prop to the `TaskModel` component so that users can select from the list of tasks.

- The `handleLinkedTasksChange` function updates the `linkedTasks` property in the form data whenever a user selects or deselects tasks from the dropdown.

- When saving the task using the "Save" button, the `formData` object will include the selected `linkedTasks`. You can then process and save this data on the server as needed.

